WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.569 --> 00:00:18.789
MCKINSEY &amp; CO:
Have you ever heard of a company McKinsey

00:00:18.789 --> 00:00:19.789
&amp; Co?

00:00:19.789 --> 00:00:25.449
They’re the oldest and largest of the “Big
Three” management consulting firms and they

00:00:25.449 --> 00:00:28.830
work with virtually every company you can
think of.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:35.100
This includes everyone from American Express
and AT&amp;T to Citibank and General Motors.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:40.750
McKinsey also offers some of the best salaries
for college graduates and offers them an exciting

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:44.850
opportunity to travel the world and work with
the largest companies.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:50.000
But, behind the hood, McKinsey isn’t all
that it’s hyped up to be.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:56.030
For one, their business in management consulting
which isn’t all that effective or useful.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:01.300
If you’re wondering why companies hire them
despite that, check out our video about that.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.340
But, being ineffective isn’t the only critic
of McKinsey.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.830
If anything, it’s actually the smallest
critic.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:14.790
The biggest red flag is that they’ve been
involved in the biggest scandals of all time

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:21.909
from Enron and the 2008 Financial Crisis to
the Opioid Epidemic and Election Scandals.

00:01:21.909 --> 00:01:25.110
And those are just to name a few.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:29.390
McKinsey has also played a role in most of
the scandals and evil businesses that Jake

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:34.430
Tran has covered even including the ones about
authoritarian regimes like Saudi Arabia and

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:35.520
Russia.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:40.820
Ironically, it seems like they’re much more
effective at helping shady nefarious projects

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:45.259
than they are when it comes to doing actual
positive management consulting.

00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:51.260
But, despite their large influence, they’re
rarely talked about on the news or social

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:52.399
media.

00:01:52.399 --> 00:01:57.180
The fact that they’re completely privately
owned just makes them even more discrete and

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.190
secretive.

00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:02.340
But, McKinsey &amp; Co wasn’t always so shady.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:07.500
Like most companies, McKinsey was established
with good intentions and for many decades,

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.700
they had a relatively clean record.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:16.120
So, here’s the story of how McKinsey &amp; Co
became the consultants that deserve hell.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:22.150
HUMBLE ORIGINS:
Taking a look back, the story of McKinsey

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:28.040
dates all the way back to 1926 to a man named
James O McKinsey.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:32.590
James was an accounting professor at the University
of Chicago, and he got the idea to create

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:37.850
McKinsey &amp; Co after witnessing a bunch of
inefficiencies across military suppliers.

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:42.090
Given that he was an accounting professor,
he felt that he could clean up their books

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.790
and make these suppliers a lot more efficient.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:49.930
So, he went ahead and established an accounting
and management firm called James O. McKinsey

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.360
&amp; Company.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:55.620
While the firm carries Jame’s name to this
day, James actually didn’t play a very big

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:59.599
role in it’s growth or expansion largely
because he couldn’t.

00:02:59.599 --> 00:03:04.590
You see, about ten years after founding the
company, James would be hit with a severe

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:07.400
case of pneumonia that took his life.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:12.420
But, on the brightside, it looks like James
had already hired a star partner named Marvin

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.810
Bower who could carry on his legacy.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:20.800
By trade, Bower was actually a lawyer, but
he never really worked as a lawyer given that

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:26.040
he joined McKinsey a few years after graduating
and he basically became the father of the

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.040
company.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:31.230
Bower established much of McKinsey’s corporate
culture and created policies that are now

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:34.120
used around the world like the “Up or Out”
policy.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:39.700
As the name suggets, if you don’t get promoted
within a certain time frame, you get fired.

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:45.170
This ensures that no employee is stagnating
or getting too comfortable, but this policy

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:50.110
has come under fire during recent times as
it also encourages backstabbing and corporate

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:51.480
politics.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:56.990
Anyway, McKinsey would drift away from it’s
accounting roots not long after James’ death.

00:03:56.990 --> 00:04:03.439
In fact, the company would physically split
up in 1939 into three companies called Scovell,

00:04:03.439 --> 00:04:07.459
Wellington, &amp; Company, McKinsey &amp; Company,
and McKinsey, Kearney &amp; Company.

00:04:07.459 --> 00:04:10.349
The accounting practice would be shifted to
Scovell, Wellington, &amp; Company which left

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:14.049
the other companies with the classic management
consulting.

00:04:14.049 --> 00:04:18.880
While this division robbed McKinsey of much
of it’s subject matter expertise, McKinsey

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.880
retained much of the military supplier relationships
that James had established.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:28.180
And this was extraordinarily valuable given
that WW2 and the Cold War were just around

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:29.180
the corner.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:33.920
McKinsey became the go to consultants for
governments, defense contractors, and military

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:38.479
organizations around the world which allowed
for exponential growth throughout the 40s

00:04:38.479 --> 00:04:39.740
and 50s.

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:45.310
They went from 88 consultants in 1951 to over
200 consultants by the 1960s.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:50.660
They were also able to establish a massive
base of operations in Europe with offices

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.169
in London, Paris, and Amsterdam.

00:04:53.169 --> 00:04:56.970
Despite all this growth, Bower never forgot
about his employees.

00:04:56.970 --> 00:05:02.150
In fact, he would constantly work to make
sure his employees were well taken care of.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:08.250
For example, in 1951, he established a profit
sharing program and in 1956 he would shift

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.980
100% of the company’s ownership to the firm’s
employees.

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:13.690
And that’s how it is to this day.

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:18.490
But, while things were developing great within
McKinsey, the same could not be said about

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:21.160
the industry and busines as a whole.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:26.570
As the era of the red scare came to an end
in the late 1960s, so did the era of the original

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:28.979
McKinsey &amp; Co.

00:05:28.979 --> 00:05:34.750
THE DEVOLUTION:
While McKinsey was highly sought after in

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:39.759
the early days due to their services being
novel and unique, the same could not be said

00:05:39.759 --> 00:05:41.580
by the 1970s.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:45.940
You see, after McKinsey ditched their accounting
roots, they never focused on another technical

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:47.080
discipline.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:51.860
And while this worked out early on, as the
industry matured, McKinsey’s services became

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:54.039
less and less valuable.

00:05:54.039 --> 00:05:58.729
Most companies preferred to hire technical
consultants with strong backgrounds in engineering,

00:05:58.729 --> 00:06:03.460
information technology, and enterprise resource
planning as opposed to generalists.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:07.860
This is why technical consulting firms like
Accenture and TCS have far outperformed the

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:10.460
legacy consultants in recent decades.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:14.120
New competition for management consulting
from firms like Boston Consulting Group and

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.919
Bain &amp; Company didn’t help the situation
either.

00:06:16.919 --> 00:06:22.400
In fact, in 1971, McKinsey’s own internal
commission found that McKinsey had become

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:26.740
too focused on geographic expansion and lacked
adequate industry knowledge.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:31.470
The commission advised that McKinsey slow
its growth and develop industry specialties.

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:36.690
Ideally, McKinsey would have specialized in
the rapidly growing tech industry, but instead,

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:40.810
they decided to specialize in various management
consulting niches.

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:44.680
This included sectors such as strategy, operations,
and organization.

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:49.800
While these sectors better defined what McKinsey
was offering, it didn’t exactly change what

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:53.669
they were offering, so they continued to face
many of the same issues.

00:06:53.669 --> 00:06:58.199
You could say that McKinsey had trouble pitching
their value proposition to companies, but

00:06:58.199 --> 00:07:03.260
they would eventually figure it out after
they analyzed what company leaders truly wanted.

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:07.740
Company leaders didn’t necessarily want
strategy or branding consulting.

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:12.870
What they really wanted was growth, happy
shareholders, a good reputation, and less

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.180
responsibility.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:18.690
McKinsey couldn’t guarantee growth or happy
shareholders, but they could help leaders

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:22.580
achieve a good reputation and less responsibility
by becoming scapegoats.

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:28.139
Are you the leader of a fortune 500 company
that needs to make a bunch of hard decisions?

00:07:28.139 --> 00:07:33.440
Well, hire us and we’ll probabaly tell you
to make the same decisions, but we can make

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:35.650
it a win win scenario for you.

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:39.099
If the choices end up working well, you can
take the praise and glory.

00:07:39.099 --> 00:07:44.680
If they don’t work on the other hand, you
can blame us and walk away relatively clean.

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:50.129
For many legacy leaders, this is a deal that’s
too good to turn down, and in modern times

00:07:50.129 --> 00:07:53.919
this is very much the real appeal of management
consultants.

00:07:53.919 --> 00:07:58.229
While this turned out to be quite lucrative
and in demand, McKinsey had regressed from

00:07:58.229 --> 00:08:03.130
being accounting experts to becoming generalists
to becoming scapegoats.

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:06.729
But this was just the beginning of their devolution.

00:08:06.729 --> 00:08:10.030
Remember how we talked about company leaders
having to make hard choices.

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:15.379
Well, these hard choices didn’t just include
completing layoffs or shutting down an underperforming

00:08:15.379 --> 00:08:16.460
sector.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:21.060
Many of these choices related to truly nefarious
activities.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:27.250
TRULY EVIL:
Before you knew it, McKinsey was knees deep

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:30.350
in shady activities and evil projects like
Enron.

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:35.240
If you’re not familiar with Enron scandal,
it was the largest accounting fraud of all

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:38.469
time leading to shareholder losses of $74
billion.

00:08:38.469 --> 00:08:44.159
The first thing we should note is that the
mastermind of the scandal, Jeff Skilling,

00:08:44.159 --> 00:08:47.660
was formerly a McKinsey consultant for 21
years.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:52.300
But, that’s just the beginning fo McKinsey’s
connection to Enron.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:58.140
Enron would use McKinsey on 20 different projects
and the two companies were so close that McKinsey

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:01.370
consultants had quote “used Enron as their
sandbox.”

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:05.970
McKinsey would never be convicted for their
connection to Enron, and while you could write

00:09:05.970 --> 00:09:11.430
off Enron as a one off connetion, McKinsey
has so many such connections that it’s hard

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:16.420
to write off everything as just a coincidence
which brings us into our next exhibit which

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:19.079
is the 2008 financial crisis.

00:09:19.079 --> 00:09:23.829
McKinsey is iconic for encouraging banks to
securitize mortgage assets and fund their

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:25.890
balance sheets using debt.

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:30.540
These practices are what would eventually
make the global financial system insolvent,

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.200
leading to the crisis.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:36.720
During this time period, McKinsey also advised
financial institutions to deliberately screw

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:38.360
over end users.

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:43.620
For example, they advised Allstate insurance
to purposely give low offers to claimants.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:48.339
The idea was that fighting this injustice
would be so expensive that lawyers would refuse

00:09:48.339 --> 00:09:50.100
to help these clients.

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:56.050
Moving on, we have likely their most disgusting
scandal as it didn’t just screw over people’s

00:09:56.050 --> 00:10:01.450
finances, it literally screwed over their
lives as their next scandal relates to the

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:02.770
opioid epidemic.

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:06.720
McKinsey created a strategy for pharmaceuticals
that would quote on quote “turbocharge”

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:08.970
sales of OxyContin.

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:13.420
This essentially consisted of McKinsey advising
pharmaceutical companies how they could actively

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:19.120
circumvent opioid regulations and deliberately
encourage and get people addicted.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:23.630
For victims of addiction, it’s common for
their close family, if they have any, to try

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:27.440
to talk to them and persuade them from an
emotional standpoint.

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:31.850
If you’ve ever been in this situation and
you’ve had trouble getting to the victim,

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:37.589
well you can blame McKinsey because they were
literally proposing strategies to counter

00:10:37.589 --> 00:10:42.010
the emotional messages from mothers with teenagers
who overdosed on OxyContin.

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:47.120
They were also proposing that pharmaceutical
companies pay pharmacies a rebate based on

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:49.700
how many overdoses and addictions they caused.

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:53.850
I mean, they literally had it down to a science.

00:10:53.850 --> 00:11:00.470
In 2019, they projected that 2,400 CVS customers
would become addicted and that each “event”,

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:06.240
which is what they called it, deserved a rebate
of $14,810.

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:11.139
This meant that Purdue Pharma would have to
pay CVS $36.8 million that year for their

00:11:11.139 --> 00:11:12.260
“work”.

00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:17.580
Fortunately, these scumbags got exposed, but
they would walk away with a settlement of

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:24.480
$573 million which is ridiculous because this
is not the type of crime that you get fined

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:25.480
for.

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:30.260
It’s the type that you get shut down for,
yet here we are.

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:34.750
At least, with this one, McKinsey wasn’t
directly causing deaths.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:40.649
With these next few cases, well, you can be
the judge.

00:11:40.649 --> 00:11:46.250
AUTHORITARIAN CONNECTIONS:
McKinsey and Saudi Arabia are basically best

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:51.850
friends given that McKinsey has completed
600 projects for Saudi Arabia between 2011

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:54.270
and 2016 alone.

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:58.600
Saudi Arabia is an authoritarian regime that
doesn’t like its citizens dissenting with

00:11:58.600 --> 00:11:59.940
the leaders.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:04.680
So, naturally, many of McKinsey’s projects
have to do with silencing dissenters.

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:10.320
Now, let me be clear, McKinsey only identifies
such individuals, they’re not involved in

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:11.830
what happens next.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:16.209
But, when you know that there’s a good chance
that the people that you identify will be

00:12:16.209 --> 00:12:22.290
unfairly arrested if not offed, it’s quite
immoral that you continue consulting for said

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:23.290
government.

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:25.920
Saudi Arabia isn’t their only authoritarian
client either.

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:28.790
Another authoritarian client is of course
China.

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:34.290
A great example of their indifferent and soulless
behavior is their behavior during the peak

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:36.680
of the Uyghur genocide in China.

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:41.290
Back in December of 2018, McKinsey hosted
a lavish company retreat alongside Chinese

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:46.579
officials while thousands of Uyghurs were
being detained and offed just miles away.

00:12:46.579 --> 00:12:51.050
McKinsey received quite a bit of public backlash
for this behavior, but it doesn’t look like

00:12:51.050 --> 00:12:52.449
they’ve changed their ways.

00:12:52.449 --> 00:12:56.840
You know how virtually every western corporation
has withdrawn from Russia due to the war?

00:12:56.840 --> 00:13:01.470
Well, it looks like McKinsey didn’t get
the memo as it’s reported that McKinsey

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:06.820
has been offering consulting services to the
Russian state owned enterprise Rostoc who’s

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:10.230
responsible for manufacturing missile engines
in the Ukraine war.

00:13:10.230 --> 00:13:14.740
What makes this even more unethical is that
McKinsey was consulting with the Pentagon

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:17.100
at the same time.

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:20.279
McKinsey also has a history of scandals with
democratic countries.

00:13:20.279 --> 00:13:24.820
For example, it’s alleged that McKinsey
helped the Gupta family to position corrupted

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:27.420
individuals across the South African government.

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:32.029
Similarly, it’s also alleged that McKinsey
helped French president Emmanual Maron to

00:13:32.029 --> 00:13:34.389
bypass campaign finance laws.

00:13:34.389 --> 00:13:39.019
And finally, it’s also alleged that McKinsey
has been helping Canada implement immigration

00:13:39.019 --> 00:13:42.950
policies that don’t have the public’s
best interest in mind.

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:49.709
A SPOT IN HELL:
Hearing all this, I don’t think I need to

00:13:49.709 --> 00:13:50.889
explain the title.

00:13:50.889 --> 00:13:55.180
While McKinsey started off with good intentions
of improving corporate accounting and management

00:13:55.180 --> 00:14:00.149
efficiency, they slowly saw their value proposition
decline decade after decade.

00:14:00.149 --> 00:14:04.190
Instead of pivoting to the technical space
which was the up and coming consulting industry,

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:06.190
they decided to turn to the darkside.

00:14:06.190 --> 00:14:11.429
They became corporate scapegoats and secret
advisors on shady strategies.

00:14:11.429 --> 00:14:15.570
These include everything from financial fraud
and corporate scandals to ruining countles

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:17.329
lives and causing deaths.

00:14:17.329 --> 00:14:22.120
Yet, given that McKinsey is a just a consulting
firm and doesn’t make the final decision,

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:27.200
they’re rarely held accountable, and even
when they are, their punishment is laughable.

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:32.430
And that’s why McKinsey &amp; Co are the consultants
that deserve hell, but that’s just what

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:33.430
I think.

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:35.240
Do you think McKinsey deserves a spot in hell?

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:36.490
Comment that down below.

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:39.949
Also, drop a like if you think McKinsey should
be held accountable.

